{% icon id="raven" size=32 /%}{% term id="glory" %}Glory{% /term %} up for grabs? The Invasion events {% term id="module" %}module{% /term %} attacks the camps of the {% term id="foreign-lord" %}Foreign Lords{% /term %} and {% term id="bloodcrow" %}Bloodcrow{% /term %} events in the {% term id="great-empire" %}Great Empire{% /term %}. Each attack earns event points and glory. The page has one tab for each event.

{% terms_on_page /%}

Turn on the tab of the event you play. The bot starts when the event starts and stops before it ends.

## How it works {% #how-it-works %}

1. When the event starts with no difficulty set, the bot sets the one in **Difficulty**.
2. It checks whether your account is under beginner or peace {% term id="protection" %}protection{% /term %}. An attack would end it, so the bot waits, as described below.
3. It finds the open camps around your {% term id="main-castle" %}main castle{% /term %} in the Great Empire, nearest first. If it finds none, it looks again every 10 minutes.
4. It takes a free {% term id="commander-game" %}commander{% /term %} from the {% ui key="client:plugins.commanderPicker.title" /%} card and attacks the camps in turn.
5. Before the first attack on a camp, it can pay to {% term id="dethrone" %}dethrone{% /term %} the camp, if you set it up.
6. After each hit lands, it reads the battle report and writes the {% term id="glory" %}glory{% /term %} of that hit, and the total for this run, to the {% term id="log" %}log{% /term %}.
7. It stops when your score reaches **Stop at this score**, or **Stop before the event ends** minutes before the end. The default is 30 minutes.

Each tab is its own {% term id="plugin" %}plugin{% /term %}, so each tab that is on counts toward your {% term id="attack-cap" %}attack cap{% /term %}.

## Difficulty {% #difficulty %}

**Difficulty** is used only when the event has no difficulty yet. **Highest unlocked without rubies** never spends {% term id="ruby" %}rubies{% /term %}, and it is the default.

{% aside type="caution" id="rented-difficulty" %}
The difficulties marked **rented with rubies** cost rubies. If you pick one and have enough rubies, the bot pays without asking. If you don't have enough, the tab stops.
{% /aside %}

## Attacking under protection {% #protection %}

By default the bot does not attack while your account has beginner or peace protection, because the attack would end it. It checks again every 30 minutes and starts once the protection is gone.

**Attack while under protection** attacks anyway.

{% aside type="caution" id="protection-ends" %}
With **Attack while under protection** on, the bot's first attack ends your beginner or peace protection. Turn it on only if you are ready to lose that protection.
{% /aside %}

## Dethrone camps {% #dethrone %}

**Dethrone camps before attacking them** pays to dethrone a camp once, before its first attack. **Exile, paid in coins**, **Exile, paid in gold tokens**, **Exile, paid in silver tokens** and **Exile, paid in samurai tokens** each cost that currency. **Fortify, paid in rubies** costs rubies. An exile needs the event to offer that currency: Bloodcrows, for example, may offer tokens and no coins. If the event doesn't, the bot writes the reason to the {% term id="log" %}log{% /term %} and attacks without dethroning. The cost grows with each dethrone, and the bot reads how many you have done from the game, so it follows the count when the game resets it. Dethrone needs your level to be 70 or higher, and the event must allow it.

Three limits keep the cost in check. The bot spends nothing until the first two are above 0.

- **Most to spend on one dethrone** is the most of the paying currency for a single dethrone.
- **Most to spend on dethrones in one event** is the total for the event.
- **Always keep at least this much of the currency that pays** is the least you keep.

## Army: Autofill or Waves {% #army %}

{% ui key="client:army.mode.waves" /%} sends exactly the {% term id="wave" %}waves{% /term %} you write, or a [virtual preset](/modules/virtual-presets/).

{% ui key="client:army.mode.autofill" /%} fills the left {% term id="flank" %}flank{% /term %}, the front and the right flank of each wave:

- **Waves with siege tools** is how many waves, from the first, carry {% term id="tool" %}siege tools{% /term %}. The default is 2.
- **Siege tools in each of those waves** picks **Wall, gate and moat** or **Wall, gate and mantlet**.
- The waves after those carry glory banners in their tool slots. **Glory banners per attack** caps them, and 0 fills all the free room. **Banner order** and **Banners to use, in order** decide which banners go first.
- **Support tools** are tools that go with the whole attack. The bot uses the first 3 on your list that you own.
- **Send a courtyard wave** fills the {% term id="courtyard" %}courtyard{% /term %} too. It is on by default.
- **Troops to keep at home** stay in the castle. The bot needs at least 100 troops to send beyond that.
- **Soldiers to send** limits the troops to those that eat food, or those that eat {% term id="mead" %}mead{% /term %}.

For the horse, **Horse** is **No horse** by default. A {% term id="coin-horse" %}coin horse{% /term %} costs coins, and a {% term id="horse-feather" %}feather{% /term %} uses one fast horse feather on each attack.

## Wave 1 from a spy report {% #spy-wave %}

**Fill wave 1 from a spy report** spies the camp before each attack and builds the first {% term id="wave" %}wave{% /term %} from what the spies saw. It works with {% ui key="client:army.mode.autofill" /%} and with {% ui key="client:army.mode.waves" /%}. The other waves stay as those build them.

1. The bot sends every spy in the castle. Your other attacks go on while the spies travel.
2. When they land, it opens the attack screen again and reads the report.
3. Wave 1 gets one ranged troop on every side: the strongest one the castle has enough of.
4. Each side gets just enough {% term id="tool" %}tools{% /term %} to break its wall, the front's gate and the defenders' ranged defence, with event and elite tools first. Wave 1 takes them before the other waves.

A feather goes only when **Horse** is **Feather** and you have one. Otherwise the spies ride the coin horse with the best spy speed when **Horse** picks any horse, and walk when it is **No horse**.

If 10 spy trips bring no report, or the castle has no spies, the bot waits 10 minutes and tries again. If the castle lacks the tools to break a wall or a gate, the bot stops and says so.

## Test with Log only {% #log-only %}

Turn on **Log only: write the attacks to the log instead of sending them**. The bot builds each attack, and each dethrone, and writes them to the {% term id="log" %}log{% /term %}. It sends nothing to the game.

